### Guide §5.2 REST API. VS Code REST Client syntax: click "Send Request" above each request.
### The app must be running on :8080 without the dev profile. The ids below (1) assume an empty
### database. Since §5.4 the data survives restarts: reset it with
### docker compose -f spring-app/compose.yaml down -v

@host = http://localhost:8080

### Create an author (201, Location: http://localhost:8080/api/authors/1)
POST {{host}}/api/authors
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Frank Herbert", "birthYear": 1920}

### Create a book (201, Location: http://localhost:8080/api/books/1). authorIds is ignored until §5.5.
POST {{host}}/api/books
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780441013593", "title": "Dune", "publishedYear": 1965, "totalCopies": 3, "authorIds": [1]}

### List books (200)
GET {{host}}/api/books

### Get one book (200)
GET {{host}}/api/books/1

### Replace the book's fields (200)
PUT {{host}}/api/books/1
Content-Type: application/json

{"isbn": "9780441013593", "title": "Dune", "publishedYear": 1965, "totalCopies": 5, "authorIds": []}

### Delete it (204)
DELETE {{host}}/api/books/1

### Get the deleted book (404)
GET {{host}}/api/books/1

### List authors (200)
GET {{host}}/api/authors

### The OpenAPI document (200); Swagger UI is at {{host}}/swagger-ui.html in a browser
GET {{host}}/v3/api-docs
